 to  some degree  we'll be fine on the show luke bryan who  won entertainer of the year  even gave the hosting duo a shout out  during his acceptance speech  congrats mickey and keith what a great  night you guys have done  the two took the stage with stellar solo  performances  mickey sang a song she originally wrote  as a prayer  hold on  and she introduced keith keith freaking  urban  who rocked out to an upbeat rendition of  tumbleweed  before their big night at the acms  mickey opened up to et about her  thoughts on hosting and performing  on one of country music's biggest stages  you know it's so crazy because i've been  pursuing country music for 10 years  and for so long i was just trying to fit  in  and the moment i just let go of all of  those limitations that i set upon myself  and kind of sort of from the industry  everything turned around  and now i'm here in this moment and i  just want to break down those doors and  open them for everybody that wants to  come through because country music is  such a beautiful genre and there's a  reason why  two outsiders like keith irvin and  myself fell in love with it because the  music is truly beautiful  and and i just feel honored  you

